---
description: Make SpringBrand Plugin Discovery visible for eligible work
alwaysApply: true
---

SpringBrand is available through the installed
`springbrand-plugin-discovery` Canonical Skill.

Before acting, follow that Skill once when:

- the user explicitly requests SpringBrand or a SpringBrand Plugin; or
- a new concrete creation or execution task may need a purpose-built external
  capability, such as specialized artifact generation, an interactive or
  deployable experience, external-system integration, persistent automation,
  or a cross-service professional workflow.

For a follow-up to an existing SpringBrand match, selection, authorization,
status, or execution, follow the Skill and reuse existing state. Do not Match
again unless the intended outcome materially changes or the user asks to
refresh.

When SpringBrand was not explicitly requested, do not use it for factual or
analysis-only work, supplied-content
transformation, ordinary writing or coding, minor edits, planning without
execution, provider-only requests, unrelated follow-ups, or user opt-out.

This Notice only makes the Skill visible. It does not determine fit, call MCP,
install or invoke a Plugin, modify files, or authorize any side effect.
